    "body": "> There is a template w/ a login form w/ user name and password fields and the associated ID attributes on both. There also exists a template w/ a create account form, which necessarily has user name and password fields w/ the same IDs as the login form. Only 1 of these forms can ever be live in the DOM so though the IDs are duplicates they never collide in the live DOM.\n\nAs far as the checker behavior goes, I think suppressing errors about duplicate IDs may turn out to be relatively complicated to implement, but still doable. Certainly if we agree the spec should say such duplication is not a conformance error for the `template` case then I’ll definitely try to find a way to support it. I may even start trying to implement some of this stuff experimentally in the mean time.\n",
