    "updated_at": "2016-01-28T09:14:37Z",
    "body": "I discussed this issue with @sideshowbarker in #whatwg a bit today\n\nhttp://logs.glob.uno/?c=freenode%23whatwg&s=28+Jan+2016&e=28+Jan+2016\n\nand we're now leaning towards not validating the `template` subtree at all, and instead focus on providing usable tools for validating the post-transformed tree (by having a validator in browsers' devtools).\n\nWe could always revisit this later and work on catching typos in attribute names and content model violations pre-transform, but right now I think my cost/benefit analysis favors skipping validation pre-transform.\n\nHTML parse errors would still be reported (e.g. `<template><table>foo</table></template>`).\n",
